00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,382
What do they want me for?

241
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:47,469
-Why did they save me?
-l'm sorry.

242
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:52,432
The angels aren't talking about it.
And it was after I fell.

243
00:14:56,813 --> 00:14:59,147
That's another question.

244
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:00,566
Why would you fall?

245
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:04,486
Why would you wanna be one of us?

246
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:07,114
-You don't mean that.
-l don't?

247
00:15:07,282 --> 00:15:10,617
A bunch of miserable bastards.
I mean, eating, crapping...

248
00:15:10,785 --> 00:15:14,955
-...confused, afraid.
-l don't know. There's loyalty.

249
00:15:15,123 --> 00:15:17,749
Forgiveness. Love.

250
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:20,085
-Pain.
-Chocolate cake.

251
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:21,795
-Guilt.
-Sex.

252
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:25,340
Yeah, you got me there.

253
00:15:28,303 --> 00:15:32,264
I mean it. Every emotion, Dean.
Even the bad ones.

254
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:36,351
It's why l fell.

255
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:41,189
It's why l'd give anything...

256
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:42,941
...not to have to go back.

257
00:15:44,819 --> 00:15:46,695
Anything.

258
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:52,701
-Feelings are overrated, if you ask me.
-Beats being an angel.

259
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:56,997
How's that possible?
You guys are powerful and perfect.

260
00:15:57,373 --> 00:16:00,542
You don't doubt yourselves.
Or God. Or anything.

261
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:03,211
Perfect. Like a marble statue.

262
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:06,381
Cold. No choice. Only obedience.

263
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:09,843
Dean, do you know how many
angels have actually seen God?

264
00:16:10,011 --> 00:16:13,472
-Seen his face?
-All of you?

265
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:15,891
Four angels.

266
00:16:16,059 --> 00:16:19,019
Four. And l'm not one of them.

267
00:16:19,187 --> 00:16:20,979
That's it?

268
00:16:22,357 --> 00:16:24,858
Well, then how do you
even know that there is a God?

269
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:28,737
We have to take it on faith,
which we're killed if we don't have.

270
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:32,115
Huh.

271
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:37,329
I was stationed on Earth 2000 years.

272
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:41,750
Just watching.

273
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:44,378
Silent.

274
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:46,380
Invisible.

275
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:49,591
Out on the road. Sick for home.

276
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:52,427
Waiting on orders from
an unknowable father...

277
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:55,222
...l can't begin to understand.
So don't tell me that--

278
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:56,765
[CHUCKLES]

279
00:16:57,183 --> 00:17:01,186
-What is so funny? What?
-Nothing, sorry. It's just....

280
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:05,732
I can relate.

281
00:17:11,239 --> 00:17:12,864
SAM:
Hey.

282
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:17,119
-Did you find something?
-l think so.

283
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:20,747
SAM: Union, Kentucky.
Found some accounts of a local miracle.

284
00:17:20,915 --> 00:17:25,460
Yeah. ln '85, there was
an empty field outside of town.

285
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:27,796
Six months later,
there was a full grown oak.

286
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:30,132
They say it looks a century old,
at least.

287
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:32,634
-Anna, what do you think?
-The grace.

288
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:37,389
Where it hit, it could have
done something like that. Easy.

289
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:40,642
So grace ground zero.
It's not destruction.

290
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,436
-lt's....
-Pure creation.

291
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:59,077
[CHUCKLES]

292
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:01,329
What?

293
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:06,752
Nothing. It's just an angel
and a demon, riding in the back seat.

294
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:08,003
[CHUCKLES]

295
00:18:08,171 --> 00:18:10,297
It's like the setup to a bad joke.

296
00:18:10,465 --> 00:18:13,091
Or a Penthouse forum letter.

297
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:17,512
Dude, reality. Porn.

298
00:18:18,306 --> 00:18:19,931
You call this reality?

299
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:33,028
It's beautiful.

300
00:18:33,196 --> 00:18:36,531
It's where the grace touched down.
I can feel it.

301
00:18:39,327 --> 00:18:42,704
-You ready to do this?
-Not really.

302
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:57,302
Anna, what are we even looking for?

303
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:10,315
It doesn't matter. It's not here.

304
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:12,067
Not anymore.

305
00:19:13,528 --> 00:19:15,070
Someone took it.

306
00:19:26,374 --> 00:19:29,584
DEAN: We still got the hex bags. I say
we head back to the panic room.

307
00:19:29,794 --> 00:19:32,087
-What, forever?
-l'm just thinking out loud.

308
00:19:32,255 --> 00:19:34,756
-You call that thinking?
-Hey, hey. Stop it.

309
00:19:34,924 --> 00:19:36,925
Anna's grace is gone,
you understand?

310
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:41,179
She can't angel up and protect us.
We can't fight heaven and hell.

311
00:19:41,347 --> 00:19:43,682
One side, maybe,
but not both. Not at once.

312
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:46,059
Guys, the angels are talking again.

313
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:50,522
-What're they saying?
-lt's weird. Like a recording.

314
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:53,942
A loop. lt says:

315
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:59,364
"Dean Winchester gives us
Anna by midnight, or...."

316
00:19:59,532 --> 00:20:01,449
Or what?

317
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:04,744
"Or we hurl him back to damnation."

318
00:20:07,832 --> 00:20:11,960
Anna, do you know of any weapon
that works on an angel?

319
00:20:12,128 --> 00:20:15,714
To what? To kill them?

320
00:20:15,882 --> 00:20:18,300
Nothing we could get to.
Not right now.

321
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:21,970
Okay, wait. I say we call Bobby,
we get him back from Hedonism....

322
00:20:22,138 --> 00:20:23,722
Dean, what's he gonna tell us?

323
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:26,600
I don't know.
But we gotta think of something.

324
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:35,650
Hey. Holding up okay?

325
00:20:35,818 --> 00:20:37,652
-Trying.
-Yeah.

326
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,946
Little scared, I guess.

327
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:44,659
So, Dean.

328
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:47,495
I just wanted to thank you.

329
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:50,081
-For what?
-Everything.

330
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:53,335
-You guys didn't have to help me--
-Hey.

331
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:57,797
Let's can the "thanks for trying"
speech, you know?

332
00:20:57,965 --> 00:21:01,176
Participation trophies suck ass.

333
00:21:01,344 --> 00:21:03,428
I don't know.

334
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:05,847
Maybe I don't deserve to be saved.

335
00:21:06,474 --> 00:21:08,516
Don't talk like that.

336
00:21:08,684 --> 00:21:13,021
I disobeyed. Lucifer disobeyed.

337
00:21:13,189 --> 00:21:15,523
It's our murder one and l knew it.

338
00:21:15,942 --> 00:21:17,692
Maybe I gotta pay.

339
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:21,780
Yeah, well, we've all
done things we got to pay for.

340
00:21:29,205 --> 00:21:31,206
I gotta tell you something.

341
00:21:31,374 --> 00:21:33,875
-You're not gonna like it.
-Okay, what?

342
00:21:34,335 --> 00:21:38,380
About a week ago,
I heard the angels talking...

343
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:42,384
...about you, what you did in hell?

344
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:44,511
Dean...

345
00:21:44,679 --> 00:21:46,429
...l know.

346
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:53,395
It wasn't your fault.

347
00:21:53,562 --> 00:21:55,355
You should forgive yourself.

348
00:21:56,524 --> 00:21:58,817
Anna, l don't wanna....

349
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:02,237
I don't wanna....

350
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:06,241
-l can't talk about that.
-l know.

351
00:22:07,243 --> 00:22:09,577
But when you can...

352
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:14,082
...you have people that wanna help.
You're not alone.

353
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,042
That's all l'm trying to say.

354
00:22:30,516 --> 00:22:32,684
What was that for?

355
00:22:32,852 --> 00:22:36,354
You know, our last night on Earth.

356
00:22:36,522 --> 00:22:38,106
All that.

357
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,280
You're stealing my best line.

358
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:08,214
Hello, Ruby.

359
00:25:09,049 --> 00:25:12,177
-Alastair.
-l have to say...

360
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:16,431
...l'm surprised to find you
out in the open like this.

361
00:25:17,266 --> 00:25:20,185
Yeah? Desperate times.

362
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:23,104
That they are.

363
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,274
You looking for this?

364
00:25:27,276 --> 00:25:29,944
Your gawky human friend
gave it to me.

365
00:25:30,154 --> 00:25:33,114
Keep it. I just came to talk.

366
00:25:33,282 --> 00:25:37,535
About what? About how a demon
is protecting an angel?

367
00:25:37,703 --> 00:25:40,455
We really must revoke
your membership.

368
00:25:40,623 --> 00:25:44,292
Look, l know l'm not
employee of the month. But this?

369
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:46,878
I never wanted to get
in the middle of this.

370
00:25:47,630 --> 00:25:50,298
-Why are you here, Ruby?
-l'll give you the angel.

371
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:54,552
-Will you? And in return?
-l walk away.

372
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:57,222
Me and the Winchester boys,
both of them.

373
00:25:57,389 --> 00:26:00,808
This angel business,
it's none of our business.

374
00:26:01,143 --> 00:26:02,560
Hmm.

375
00:26:03,938 --> 00:26:08,316
You know,
I'd always heard that you were...

376
00:26:08,484 --> 00:26:11,986
...a devious, cowardly little slut.

377
00:26:12,196 --> 00:26:14,072
You don't disappoint.

378
00:26:17,076 --> 00:26:20,995
-So, what do you say?
-lt's interesting. Prudent.

379
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,834
[GASPS]

380
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:30,171
But...

381
00:26:30,339 --> 00:26:33,758
...let me make you...

382
00:26:33,926 --> 00:26:36,010
...a counteroffer.

383
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:39,639
[DOOR CREAKS]

384
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:45,937
URIEL:
Look at that.

385
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:48,856
So cute the monkeys wear clothes.

386
00:26:56,282 --> 00:26:59,784
-l'm dreaming, aren't I?
-lt's the only way we could chat.

387
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:03,538
Since you're hiding like cowards.

388
00:27:03,706 --> 00:27:06,207
Don't normally see you off leash.
Where's your boss?

389
00:27:06,375 --> 00:27:09,544
Castiel? Oh, he's....

390
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:14,215
He's not here. You see,
he has this weakness. He likes you.

391
00:27:16,719 --> 00:27:19,804
Time's up, boy. We want the girl.

392
00:27:19,972 --> 00:27:23,558
Wouldn't try that if l were you.
See, she got her grace back.

393
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:26,394
Full-blown angel now.

394
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:28,730
That would be a neat trick, considering...

395
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:32,400
...l have her grace right here.

396
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:36,529
We can't let hell
get their hooks into her.

397
00:27:36,697 --> 00:27:38,990
Why don't you give her back
her angel juice?

398
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:42,577
-She committed a serious crime.
-What? Thinking for herself?

399
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:46,414
This is our business, not yours.
She's not even human, not technically.

400
00:27:46,582 --> 00:27:50,084
I guess I just like being
a pain in the pooper.

401
00:27:51,503 --> 00:27:52,879
No.

402
00:27:54,340 --> 00:27:56,257
There's more.

403
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:02,388
[CHUCKLES]

404
00:28:02,806 --> 00:28:05,767
You cut yourself a slice of...

405
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:08,770
...angel-food cake.

406
00:28:08,937 --> 00:28:11,939
Didn't you? Huh? You did.

407
00:28:12,107 --> 00:28:13,775
[LAUGHS]

408
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:16,694
What do you care?
You're junk-less down there...

409
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:20,073
-...like a Ken doll?
-Hoo-hoo-hoo.

410
00:28:20,783 --> 00:28:24,744
Well, it's your last chance.

411
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,455
-Give us the girl or....
-Or what?

412
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:31,209
What,
you'll toss me back in the hole?

413
00:28:32,294 --> 00:28:35,088
-You're bluffing.
-Try me.

414
00:28:36,924 --> 00:28:40,802
It's a whole lot bigger than
the plans we have for you, Dean.

415
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:42,720
You can be replaced.

416
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:54,148
What the hell?

417
00:28:55,234 --> 00:28:56,776
Go ahead and do it.

418
00:29:05,411 --> 00:29:08,079
You're just crazy enough to go,
aren't you?

419
00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:10,623
What can I say? l don't break easy.

420
00:29:12,501 --> 00:29:13,751
Oh, yes.

421
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:19,924
You do.

422
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:25,680
You just gotta know
where to apply the right pressure.

423
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:32,103
[MUFFLED SCREAMlNG]

424
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:34,355
[SLlCING]

425
00:29:35,149 --> 00:29:36,607
[WHlMPERlNG]

426
00:29:36,817 --> 00:29:40,153
ALASTAlR: You know the problem
with your generation?

427
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:44,532
Instant gratification.
It's all now, now, now.

428
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:48,953
No patience, no craftsmanship.

429
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:55,960
But l do have to say, this knife of yours...

430
00:29:56,128 --> 00:29:59,464
...it's an exquisite piece.

431
00:29:59,631 --> 00:30:01,841
You must tell me where you found it.

432
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:05,219
[GROANING]

433
00:30:05,429 --> 00:30:08,389
You know, I haven't been up here...

434
00:30:08,557 --> 00:30:10,725
...since Poland, '43.

435
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:12,310
[SLlCING AND SCREAMlNG RESUME]

436
00:30:12,478 --> 00:30:14,395
Truth is, l loathe it. lt's chilly.

437
00:30:14,563 --> 00:30:17,231
No stink of blood or sizzle of flesh.

438
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:20,902
Or the wet flap of flayed skin.
I don't know how you stand it.

439
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:24,739
So sooner you cooperate,
the sooner l can finish up...

440
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:29,994
...with this ghastly angel business
and return home to my studies.

441
00:30:31,580 --> 00:30:35,458
But no rush. Let's take our time.

442
00:30:36,585 --> 00:30:38,920
Relish the moment.

443
00:30:40,881 --> 00:30:44,217
Now, l'm going to remove this...

444
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:46,260
...don't go smoking out of that meat.

445
00:30:46,428 --> 00:30:49,013
You won't get very far.

446
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:53,726
[GASPlNG]

447
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:58,856
Now you tell me where that angel is.

448
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:02,360
-No.
-No?

449
00:31:04,530 --> 00:31:06,113
No.

450
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:09,575
I tell you...

451
00:31:09,743 --> 00:31:11,369
...you kill me.

452
00:31:14,289 --> 00:31:16,207
But l'll show you.

453
00:31:16,792 --> 00:31:18,376
[CHUCKLES]

454
00:31:28,762 --> 00:31:31,889
I don't know, man. Where's Ruby?

455
00:31:32,057 --> 00:31:34,141
Hey, she's your hell buddy.

456
00:31:36,937 --> 00:31:38,813
It's a little early for that, isn't it?

457
00:31:39,648 --> 00:31:40,815
[EXHALES]

458
00:31:41,024 --> 00:31:42,567
It's 2 a.m. somewhere.

459
00:31:43,652 --> 00:31:46,153
-You okay?
-Yeah, of course.

460
00:31:46,321 --> 00:31:48,114
[WlND HOWLlNG]

461
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:02,169
Hello, Anna. lt's good to see you.

462
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:06,048
How? How did you find us?

463
00:32:18,103 --> 00:32:19,562
Dean?

464
00:32:21,023 --> 00:32:22,440
I'm sorry.

465
00:32:22,983 --> 00:32:24,483
Why?

466
00:32:28,614 --> 00:32:31,157
Because they gave him a choice.

467
00:32:31,325 --> 00:32:34,535
They either kill me or kill you.

468
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,080
I know how their minds work.

469
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:57,350
You did the best you could.

470
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:00,227
I forgive you.

471
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:12,657
Okay, no more tricks.

472
00:33:14,826 --> 00:33:16,827
No more running.

473
00:33:20,415 --> 00:33:21,832
I'm ready.

474
00:33:29,841 --> 00:33:31,509
I'm sorry.

475
00:33:31,677 --> 00:33:34,720
No. You're not.

476
00:33:34,930 --> 00:33:38,641
Not really.
You don't know the feeling.

477
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:43,604
Still, we have a history. lt's just....

478
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:46,732
Orders are orders. I know.

479
00:33:46,942 --> 00:33:49,193
Just make it quick.

480
00:33:52,447 --> 00:33:56,450
Don't you touch a hair
on that poor girl's head.

481
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:09,547
How dare you come in this room...

482
00:34:10,090 --> 00:34:12,591
...you pussing sore?

483
00:34:13,343 --> 00:34:15,261
Name-calling?

484
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:17,680
That hurt my feelings.

485
00:34:17,848 --> 00:34:20,850
You sanctimonious, fanatical prick.

486
00:34:21,017 --> 00:34:23,060
Turn around and walk away now.

487
00:34:23,228 --> 00:34:25,396
Sure. Just give us the girl.

488
00:34:26,148 --> 00:34:29,066
We'll make sure
she gets punished good and proper.

489
00:34:29,985 --> 00:34:32,987
You know who we are
and what we will do.

490
00:34:35,866 --> 00:34:37,825
I won't say it again.

491
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:42,621
Leave now or we lay you to waste.

492
00:34:43,165 --> 00:34:44,790
Think l'll take my chances.

493
00:34:52,299 --> 00:34:54,383
[GRUNTlNG]

494
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:05,853
Sorry, kiddo.
Why don't you go run to Daddy?

495
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:12,693
[SCREAMS]

496
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:18,532
[SPEAKING IN LATIN]

497
00:35:26,249 --> 00:35:27,583
[GRUNTS]

498
00:35:30,295 --> 00:35:34,256
ALASTAlR: Dean, Dean, Dean.
I am so disappointed.

499
00:35:34,424 --> 00:35:37,635
You had such promise.

500
00:35:39,221 --> 00:35:41,972
[BOTH GASPlNG, GRUNTlNG]

501
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:51,190
-No!
-Uhn!

502
00:35:54,569 --> 00:35:56,153
[GASPlNG]

503
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,618
[GRUNTS]

504
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:08,624
ANNA:
Shut your eyes.

505
00:36:08,792 --> 00:36:10,167
Shut your eyes.

506
00:36:14,673 --> 00:36:17,132
Shut your eyes!

507
00:36:17,342 --> 00:36:19,510
[SCREAMlNG]

508
